DFG constant folding called Math.* C functions through a deduced template argument, which drops
the VFP calling-convention attribute on softfp ARMv7: Math.log(10) folded to NaN, sin/cos/exp wrong.

--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/dfg/DFGAbstractInterpreterInlines.h
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/dfg/DFGAbstractInterpreterInlines.h
@@ -1556,7 +1556,13 @@
         break;
 
     case ArithUnary:
-        executeDoubleUnaryOpEffects(node, arithUnaryFunction(node->arithUnaryType()));
+        {
+            // softfp ARMv7: a function pointer passed as a deduced template argument loses its
+            // pcs("aapcs-vfp") attribute, so the call would pass the double in r0:r1 while the
+            // function reads d0. Calling through the typed pointer in a lambda keeps the VFP ABI.
+            Arith::UnaryFunction function = arithUnaryFunction(node->arithUnaryType());
+            executeDoubleUnaryOpEffects(node, [function](double value) -> double { return function(value); });
+        }
         break;
             
     case ToBoolean:
